# Mintlify deployment (T3Planet Docs)

## 🚨 Permission gate

No push to GitHub and no Mintlify production publish unless the operator says exactly **`start the deployment process`**. Default is local-only. See `.cursor/rules/deployment-permission-gate.mdc`.

Live site: https://docs.t3planet.de/en/latest  
Mintlify project: **T3Planet Docs** (workspace **nitsan-81630f36**)

## Connected GitHub (source of live builds)

**Use only the organization repository** for deployment:

- Live / deploy source: **`nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs`** branch `master`
- Local remote name: **`origin`** → `https://github.com/nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs.git`

Do **not** use `markus-neumannn/T3Planet-docs` (or any personal fork) as the normal deploy target.

Mintlify dashboard **Git** settings must point at **`nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs`** (`master`). If Git settings still show a fork, live will not follow `origin` pushes — reconnect Git in the Mintlify dashboard.

### Author vs repository (do not confuse)

- **Commit author:** **Nitsan** `<sanjay@nitsantech.com>`
- **Push remote:** always **`origin`** → `nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs`
- A personal GitHub **fork** is never the day-to-day production source

### Emergency live unblock

If the operator needs live **now** and Mintlify Activity still shows a personal fork:

1. Prefer reconnecting Mintlify Git to the org repo.
2. If reconnect is blocked and live is urgent: temporarily add the fork remote, `git push <fork-remote> origin/master:master` (same SHA already on org — no force), poll live until content matches, then remove the temporary remote.
3. Tell the operator clearly this was an emergency sync because Mintlify Git was still on the fork.

For normal releases:

1. Commit as **Nitsan** (email above) via env — do not invent credentials.
2. `git fetch` / safe sync, then `git push origin HEAD:master`
3. Confirm Mintlify **Activity** + spot-check live HTML (not HTTP 200 alone).

Full procedure: `docs/deployment/deploy.md` and repo `.cursor/context.md`.

## Custom domain & SSL (do not break live)

Production domain: **`docs.t3planet.de`** (base path `/en/latest`).

**Never** delete/recreate the Cloudflare custom hostname or remove the custom domain to clear CDN/edge cache. That wiped SSL on 2026-09-25 and took the main docs URL offline (`ERR_SSL_VERSION_OR_CIPHER_MISMATCH`) until ACME DNS was updated.

For stale custom-domain pages: verify origin (`t3planet.mintlify.app`), wait for deploy, hard-refresh, or fix content via Git. Full rules: `.cursor/rules/custom-domain-ssl-safety.mdc`.

## Local tooling

- Node **20** for `mintlify` / `mint` (Node 25+ unsupported).
- After nav/page count changes: `python3 scripts/compute_doc_stats.py`.
- Do not commit `RST Format */` or `scripts/remigration/*` QA dumps unless explicitly requested.
- Do not commit or push `workshops/` or `docs-master/` (`backup/` is mintignored).
